    "review_markdown": "Your portfolio fell 1.16% in the week to 1 Oct, 0.41 points behind DSEX; BXPHARMA's 14.88% fall explains most of it.\n\n- BXPHARMA fell 14.88%, 11.89 points against its sector index, so the move was its own, not the sector's. It came after quarterly results on 27 Sep reporting EPS of Tk 1.62 against Tk 2.41 for the same quarter last year. It contributed -7968 BDT and -1.24 points to the portfolio, the largest move of the week. [q:e3d3b745-337e-46d5-9d0a-8ad385846375] [q:95042254-0c10-4d19-8a42-18e05fb872d9]\n- SQURPHARMA is 25.4% of the portfolio, above your 25% position limit. [q:dd4fc22a-140c-4c79-af7c-efd01744024e]\n- Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals is 37.8% of the portfolio, 7.8 points above your 30% target. [q:dd4fc22a-140c-4c79-af7c-efd01744024e]\n\n**What I remembered**\n\n**What to look at next**\n- SQURPHARMA weight against 25% limit\n- Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals weight against 30% target\n\nNot covered: GP buy target 358.80 vs LTP 355.00\n\nThis is a review of your own records, not financial advice.",
